Available Commands:
  avenue       record a line of inquiry and its fate: --line "<the question or approach>" --status declined|abandoned|pursued --reason "<why not taken, or what killed it>" [--method "<the source class or technique>"]
  closing      a ### BLUE CLOSING entry per docketed gap: --id <gap> --file <prose>
  confidence   per-claim confidence (the calibration substrate): --claim <claim-label> --confidence high|medium|low
  dispute      contest a grade through the accounted channel: --id <gap> --dimension severity|likelihood|impact|complexity_cost --proposed <grade> --basis "..."
  friction     attributed friction (survives aborts as an event): --text|--file
  manifest-row one correctness-manifest receipt per repaired gap: --id R2-3 --row "figures recomputed; acceptance check run: pass; sites swept: S2,S4"
  petition     petition the bench (never sanctioned; does not pause your duties): --petition-class ethical|safety|integrity|constitutional --basis "..." --relief "..."
  position     the round's ### BLUE section (prose via --file)
  register     FIRST ACTION at the seat: register --run <runDir> --seat-id <SEAT_ID from your prompt>
  render       read-only projection refresh (any seat may invoke)
  retire       remove a claim from the report, on the record: --claim "<the claim, quoted>" --reason "..." [--superseded-by "<the claim that replaces it>"]
  revision     the round-record event (the CHANGELOG entry body via --file) — singleton per seat-round; emit AFTER your report edits land
  show         read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification): --view board|ledger|archive|debate|changelog|citation-ledger|lines-of-inquiry

