Usage:
  {TOOL} [flags]
  {TOOL} [command]

Available Commands:
  assemble      assemble <run>/report.md from the record — blue's audited sections lifted verbatim, the rest composed from the event log; no inputs
  certify       the run-end certification statement ("what I would want a human to re-examine"): --file <statement>
  friction      attributed friction (the bench seats had no event path before — the abort-surviving copy): --text|--file
  halt          the safety boundary: --file <written opinion — capture relays it like a FAIL, never smoothed>
  opinion       a ruling as an OPINION: --id R3-2 --as carried|closed|... --principle "..." --tension "correctness vs economy" --review-flag "why a human should look" [--file rationale]
  outcome       record the run's terminal verdict as a fact: --as VERIFIED|CEILING|HALTED|UNVERIFIED [--deadlocked] [--exhausted]
  petition-rule rule on a petition: --petitioner <seatId> --petition-class <class> --as granted|denied --file <opinion> (a halt is its own verb)
  register      FIRST ACTION at the sitting: register --run <runDir> --seat-id <SEAT_ID from your prompt>
  render        read-only projection refresh (any seat may invoke)
  show          read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification): --view board|ledger|archive|debate|changelog|citation-ledger|lines-of-inquiry

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for bench

Global Flags:
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory (the engine passes it; it is in your prompt)
      --seat-id string   your seat id, assigned by the engine and bound to this role's namespace

